dense and sparse cases\n- Update the docstring to reflect the new sparse parameter and behavior\n- Add tests for the sparse output functionality\n\nThese locations form the minimal set of changes needed to implement the requested feature while maintaining backward compatibility.", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "user", "content": "Verify if the found locations contain all the necessary information to address the issue, and check for any relevant references in other parts of the codebase that may not have appeared in the search results. If not, continue searching for additional locations related to the issue.\nVerify that you have carefully analyzed the impact of the found locations on the repository, especially their dependencies. If you think you have solved the task, rewrite your final answer into the required location-only format, output ONLY the location block, and then call `finish` to finish.\nIMPORTANT: YOU SHOULD NEVER ASK FOR HUMAN HELP.\nDaLIC raw evidence tools remain available throughout the investigation.\nIf your current evidence is either too broad, too few or incomplete, call `get_trace_artifacts` or `get_trace_data_dependencies` again with more precise filters before finishing.\n"}, {"content": "Let me verify the completeness of the found locations and analyze their dependencies more thoroughly.\n\nFirst, let's check for any additional dependencies related to sparse matrices:\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=search_terms>['scipy.sparse', 'sparse matrix']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OBSERVATION:\nsklearn/preprocessing/_data.py:binarize\nsklearn/preprocessing/_polynomial.py:_create_expansion\nsklearn/neighbors/_base.py:_check_precomputed\nsklearn/metrics/pairwise.py:paired_distances\nsklearn/metrics/pairwise.py:linear_kernel\nsklearn/metrics/pairwise.py:pa