window.Rolling.quantile : Calculate the rolling quantile.\n2571 |         numpy.percentile : Returns the q-th percentile(s) of the array elements.\n2572 | \n2573 |         Examples\n2574 |         --------\n2575 |         >>> s = pd.Series([1, 2, 3, 4])\n2576 |         >>> s.quantile(0.5)\n2577 |         2.5\n2578 |         >>> s.quantile([0.25, 0.5, 0.75])\n2579 |         0.25    1.75\n2580 |         0.50    2.50\n2581 |         0.75    3.25\n2582 |         dtype: float64\n2583 |         \"\"\"\n2584 |         validate_percentile(q)\n2585 | \n2586 |         # We dispatch to DataFrame so that core.internals only has to worry\n2587 |         #  about 2D cases.\n2588 |         df = self.to_frame()\n2589 | \n2590 |         result = df.quantile(q=q, interpolation=interpolation, numeric_only=False)\n2591 |         if result.ndim == 2:\n2592 |             result = result.iloc[:, 0]\n2593 | \n2594 |         if is_list_like(q):\n2595 |             result.name = self.name\n2596 |             idx = Index(q, dtype=np.float64)\n2597 |             return self._constructor(result, index=idx, name=self.name)\n2598 |         else:\n2599 |             # scalar\n2600 |             return result.iloc[0]\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/core/arrays/masked.py:BaseMaskedArray._accumulate`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n1563 | def _accumulate(\n1564 |         self, name: str, *, skipna: bool = True, **kwargs\n1565 |     ) -> BaseMaskedArray:\n1566 |         data = self._data\n1567 |         mask = self._mask\n1568 | \n1569 |         op = getattr(masked_accumulations, name)\n1570 |         data, mask = op(data, mask, skipna=skipna, **kwargs)\n1571 | \n1572 |         return self._simple_new(data, mask)\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/core/resample.py:Resampler.interpolate`.\nFound function `pandas/core/internals/blocks.py:Block.interpolate`.\nFound function `pandas/core/internals/managers.py:BaseBlockManager.interpolate`.\nFound function `pandas/core/arrays